\par\b\f1\fs38 Dashboard Technical Design\b0\fs22\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs30 Purpose\b0\fs22\par
\par
This document explains how the DRCS executive dashboard is built, what each visible KPI means, and how developers should implement or extend dashboard metrics safely.\par
\par
This dashboard is not a generic BI surface. It is a workflow-oriented readiness cockpit for:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab UAE eInvoicing readiness\par
\tab\bullet\tab PINT-AE conformance\par
\tab\bullet\tab source data quality\par
\tab\bullet\tab exception prioritisation\par
\tab\bullet\tab regulator-facing implementation explainability\par
\par
Primary implementation sources:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `src/pages/DashboardPage.tsx`\par
\tab\bullet\tab `src/hooks/useDashboardMetrics.ts`\par
\tab\bullet\tab `src/context/ComplianceContext.tsx`\par
\tab\bullet\tab `src/constants/dashboardLabels.ts`\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs30 Design Principles\b0\fs22\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab Explainability over visual noise\par
\tab\bullet\tab Distinguish document-level readiness from rule-level performance\par
\tab\bullet\tab Prefer deterministic calculations over inferred percentages\par
\tab\bullet\tab Make scope absence explicit when a KPI is not applicable\par
\tab\bullet\tab Keep regulator-facing and operational language separate where needed\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs30 Page Architecture\b0\fs22\par
\par
The dashboard is currently assembled directly inside `src/pages/DashboardPage.tsx`.\par
\par
High-level structure:\par
\par
1. Context strip\par
2. Executive compliance KPIs\par
3. Data quality KPIs\par
4. UAE-specific compliance coverage\par
5. Exception breakdown and remediation focus\par
\par
Runtime data flow:\par
\par
1. `useCompliance()` supplies:\par
   - `headers`\par
   - `buyers`\par
   - `lines`\par
   - `checkResults`\par
   - `exceptions`\par
   - `getDashboardStats()`\par
2. `buildDashboardSnapshot()` normalises the active scope into a single `DashboardSnapshot`\par
3. `computeDashboardMetrics()` provides document-vs-rule metric separation\par
4. UI cards render from the snapshot\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs30 Source Layers\b0\fs22\par
\par
The dashboard combines three source layers:\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 1. Raw portfolio data\b0\fs22\par
\par
Used for:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab invoice counts\par
\tab\bullet\tab completeness metrics\par
\tab\bullet\tab null-rate quality\par
\tab\bullet\tab duplicate ratio\par
\tab\bullet\tab currency mismatch logic\par
\tab\bullet\tab credit-note scenario coverage\par
\par
Primary sources:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `headers`\par
\tab\bullet\tab `buyers`\par
\tab\bullet\tab `lines`\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 2. Validation run outputs\b0\fs22\par
\par
Used for:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab rule outcomes\par
\tab\bullet\tab rule pass rate\par
\tab\bullet\tab submission-ready invoice count\par
\tab\bullet\tab critical blocker outcomes\par
\tab\bullet\tab blocker document counts\par
\par
Primary sources:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `checkResults`\par
\tab\bullet\tab `exceptions`\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 3. Context-level summary stats\b0\fs22\par
\par
Used as fallback or compatibility support.\par
\par
Primary source:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `getDashboardStats()` from `ComplianceContext`\par
\par
Important limitation:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `getDashboardStats().passRate` is legacy-like and document-oriented in `ComplianceContext`\par
\tab\bullet\tab `computeDashboardMetrics().rulePassRate` is the current rule-outcome-level metric\par
\tab\bullet\tab developers must not collapse these two layers back into one percentage\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs30 Dashboard Snapshot Contract\b0\fs22\par
\par
The page works from a single in-memory object:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `DashboardSnapshot`\par
\par
Key categories inside the snapshot:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab scope context\par
\tab\bullet\tab readiness scores\par
\tab\bullet\tab executive KPI values\par
\tab\bullet\tab data quality KPI values\par
\tab\bullet\tab UAE coverage values\par
\tab\bullet\tab exception aggregation\par
\tab\bullet\tab remediation prioritisation\par
\par
This snapshot should remain the source of truth for rendering.\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs30 Metric Logic\b0\fs22\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs30 1. Context Strip\b0\fs22\par
\par
These values appear in the top strip above the KPI cards.\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 Document flow\b0\fs22\par
\par
Meaning:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab current dataset direction in scope\par
\par
Value:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `AR / Outbound` when `activeDatasetType === 'AR'`\par
\tab\bullet\tab `AP / Inbound` otherwise\par
\par
Source:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab UI state, not a computed KPI\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 Live portfolio snapshot\b0\fs22\par
\par
Meaning:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab indicates checks have been run on the currently loaded portfolio\par
\par
Logic:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `Live portfolio snapshot` if `isChecksRun === true`\par
\tab\bullet\tab `Live data loaded` otherwise\par
\par
Source field:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `snapshot.modeLabel`\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 Executive attention required\b0\fs22\par
\par
Meaning:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab headline status badge for the current scope\par
\par
Logic:\par
\par
1. `Validation running` when `isRunning === true`\par
2. `Executive attention required` when `snapshot.criticalIssues > 0`\par
3. `Executive ready` otherwise\par
\par
Interpretation:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab this is a status badge, not a numeric KPI\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 Invoices in scope\b0\fs22\par
\par
Meaning:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab number of invoices included in the active dashboard scope\par
\par
Formula:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `stats.totalInvoices || headerRecords.length`\par
\par
Source:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `buildDashboardSnapshot()`\par
\par
Fallback:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab falls back to header count if summary stats are absent\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 Rule outcomes\b0\fs22\par
\par
Meaning:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab total number of individual rule evaluations executed\par
\par
Formula:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `sum(checkResult.passed + checkResult.failed)`\par
\par
Source:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `computeDashboardMetrics().totalRuleOutcomes`\par
\par
Important:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab one invoice generates many rule outcomes\par
\tab\bullet\tab this is not a document count\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 Critical blockers\b0\fs22\par
\par
Meaning:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab count of critical exception outcomes currently represented in the active scope\par
\par
Current logic in context strip:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `snapshot.criticalIssues`\par
\par
Current formula:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `stats.exceptionsBySeverity.Critical || scopedCriticalExceptionCount`\par
\par
Interpretation warning:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab this is currently an outcome-oriented critical count, not a distinct document count\par
\tab\bullet\tab use `criticalBlockerDocumentCount` and `avgCriticalBlockersPerDocument` when explaining operational burden\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs30 2. Executive Compliance KPIs\b0\fs22\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 Go-Live Readiness\b0\fs22\par
\par
Meaning:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab blended executive confidence score for controlled production readiness\par
\par
Formula:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `clampScore(weightedAverage(goLiveInputs))`\par
\par
Dimensions and weights:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `40%` compliance score\par
\tab\bullet\tab `15%` null-rate quality\par
\tab\bullet\tab `10%` duplicate control\par
\tab\bullet\tab `10%` currency alignment\par
\tab\bullet\tab `15%` blocker containment\par
\tab\bullet\tab `10%` credit-note readiness\par
\par
Component formulas:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab compliance score = `complianceReadiness`\par
\tab\bullet\tab null-rate quality = `max(0, 100 - nullFieldRate * 4)`\par
\tab\bullet\tab duplicate control = `max(0, 100 - duplicateInvoiceRatio * 18)`\par
\tab\bullet\tab currency alignment = `max(0, 100 - ((currencyMismatchCount / totalInvoices) * 180))`\par
\tab\bullet\tab blocker containment = `max(0, 100 - min(criticalIssues, 10) * 12)`\par
\tab\bullet\tab credit-note readiness = `creditNote.coverage` when credit notes exist, else `100`\par
\par
Band logic:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `>= 90` Ready\par
\tab\bullet\tab `75 to 89` Watch\par
\tab\bullet\tab `< 75` Blocked\par
\par
Important:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab this is a product score, not a regulatory formula\par
\tab\bullet\tab treat it as a blended decision-support KPI\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 Compliance Readiness\b0\fs22\par
\par
Meaning:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab weighted structural and validation readiness baseline\par
\par
Formula:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `clampScore(weightedAverage(readinessInputs))`\par
\par
Dimensions and weights:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `35%` mandatory data\par
\tab\bullet\tab `15%` conditional data\par
\tab\bullet\tab `30%` rule conformance\par
\tab\bullet\tab `20%` blocker pressure\par
\par
Component formulas:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab mandatory data = average of header, buyer, and line completeness\par
\tab\bullet\tab conditional data = conditional completeness percentage\par
\tab\bullet\tab rule conformance = rule pass rate\par
\tab\bullet\tab blocker pressure = `max(0, 100 - min(criticalIssues, 10) * 10)`\par
\par
Important:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab this score excludes null-rate, duplication, and FX alignment penalties that are used in Go-Live Readiness\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 Submission-ready invoices\b0\fs22\par
\par
Meaning:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab count of invoices that pass every executed rule check in the active scope\par
\par
Display:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `submissionReadyCount / totalInvoices`\par
\par
Formula:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `submissionReadyCount = max(totalInvoicesInScope - failedInvoiceIds.size, 0)`\par
\tab\bullet\tab `submissionReadyRate = submissionReadyCount / totalInvoicesInScope`\par
\par
Source:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `computeDashboardMetrics()`\par
\par
How failed invoices are identified:\par
\par
1. use invoice-linked failed exceptions from `checkResults[].exceptions` when available\par
2. fall back to invoice-linked `exceptions`\par
\par
Important:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab this is the primary document-level go/no-go signal\par
\tab\bullet\tab do not derive this from rule pass rate\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 Rule pass rate\b0\fs22\par
\par
Meaning:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab proportion of executed rule outcomes that passed\par
\par
Display:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab percentage only\par
\par
Formula:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `passedRuleOutcomes / totalRuleOutcomes`\par
\par
Source:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `computeDashboardMetrics()`\par
\par
Important:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab this is a rule-engine performance metric\par
\tab\bullet\tab one failing rule on one invoice can still leave rule pass rate high while making that invoice not submission-ready\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 Critical Blocking Issues\b0\fs22\par
\par
Meaning:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab currently rendered as count of critical issues in active scope\par
\par
Source:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `snapshot.criticalIssues`\par
\par
Current formula:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `stats.exceptionsBySeverity.Critical || scopedCriticalExceptionCount`\par
\par
Important distinction:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab this card is not yet using `criticalBlockerDocumentCount`\par
\tab\bullet\tab when evolving the dashboard, developers should decide whether the card should continue to represent:\par
  - critical outcomes\par
  - critical exception cases\par
  - affected documents\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs30 3. Data Quality KPIs\b0\fs22\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 Mandatory Field Completeness\b0\fs22\par
\par
Meaning:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab average completeness across core required fields\par
\par
Formula:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab average of:\par
  - header completeness\par
  - buyer completeness\par
  - line completeness\par
\par
Completeness formula per group:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab present mandatory values / total mandatory field slots\par
\par
Source field groups:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab header: `MANDATORY_HEADER_FIELDS`\par
\tab\bullet\tab buyer: `MANDATORY_BUYER_FIELDS`\par
\tab\bullet\tab line: `MANDATORY_LINE_FIELDS`\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 Conditional Field Completeness\b0\fs22\par
\par
Meaning:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab completeness across scenario-triggered requirements only\par
\par
Formula:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab satisfied conditional requirements / triggered conditional requirements\par
\par
Triggered conditions currently include:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab positive `amount_due` -> `payment_due_date`\par
\tab\bullet\tab non-AED invoice currency -> `fx_rate` and `tax_currency = AED`\par
\tab\bullet\tab invoice type `381` -> credit note fields\par
\tab\bullet\tab buyer name present -> `buyer_trn`\par
\par
Scope-absent logic:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab if `qualifyingDocumentCount === 0`, the card renders `Not in scope`\par
\par
Important:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab zero qualifying documents is not a failure\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 Null Field Rate\b0\fs22\par
\par
Meaning:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab percentage of evaluated governed fields that are empty\par
\par
Formula:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab empty governed field slots / total governed field slots evaluated\par
\par
Important:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab lower is better\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 Duplicate Invoice Ratio\b0\fs22\par
\par
Meaning:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab duplicate incidence in the invoice header population\par
\par
Formula:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab duplicate invoice records / total header records\par
\par
Current duplicate logic:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab key = `invoice_number` or fallback `invoice_id`\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 Invalid Codelist\b0\fs22\par
\par
Meaning:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab count of open exceptions that appear to be codelist-related\par
\par
Current logic:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab text classification over exception name, message, and check id\par
\par
Current search terms:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `codelist`\par
\tab\bullet\tab `code`\par
\tab\bullet\tab `iso3166`\par
\tab\bullet\tab `uncl`\par
\tab\bullet\tab `unece`\par
\tab\bullet\tab `currency`\par
\tab\bullet\tab `payment means`\par
\par
Important:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab this is heuristic, not registry-driven\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 Currency Mismatches\b0\fs22\par
\par
Meaning:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab header-level count of currency / tax-currency / FX inconsistencies\par
\par
Logic:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab for AED invoices:\par
  - mismatch if `tax_currency` is populated but not `AED`\par
\tab\bullet\tab for non-AED invoices:\par
  - mismatch if `tax_currency !== AED`\par
  - or `fx_rate` missing / non-numeric / non-positive\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs30 4. UAE-Specific Compliance Coverage\b0\fs22\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 IBT Mandatory Fields\b0\fs22\par
\par
Meaning:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab coverage of mandatory invoice business-term fields\par
\par
Current implementation:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab mirrors `mandatoryCompleteness`\par
\par
Supporting points shown:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab header completeness\par
\tab\bullet\tab buyer completeness\par
\tab\bullet\tab line completeness\par
\par
Important:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab this is a coverage proxy, not a full formal semantic mapping audit\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 PINT-AE Rules\b0\fs22\par
\par
Meaning:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab rule execution and rule pass performance for the selected scope\par
\par
Current value:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab same percentage as rule pass rate\par
\par
Supporting points:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab total rule outcomes executed\par
\tab\bullet\tab current pass rate\par
\tab\bullet\tab critical issues still blocking\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 Credit-Note Scenarios\b0\fs22\par
\par
Meaning:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab readiness of in-scope `381` credit note scenarios\par
\par
Coverage logic:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab if no credit notes are present:\par
  - `count = 0`\par
  - coverage defaults to `100`\par
\tab\bullet\tab if credit notes are present:\par
  - each credit note must satisfy:\par
    - reason code\par
    - reason text\par
    - preceding reference unless reason code is `VD`\par
    - preceding issue date unless reason code is `VD`\par
\par
Important:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab when no credit notes are present, this behaves as not-applicable rather than failed\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs30 5. Exception Breakdown and Remediation\b0\fs22\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 Severity cards\b0\fs22\par
\par
Meaning:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab counts of open exceptions by severity\par
\par
Formula:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab count scoped exceptions where severity equals:\par
  - `Critical`\par
  - `High`\par
  - `Medium`\par
  - `Low`\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 Top blocking issues\b0\fs22\par
\par
Meaning:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab top recurring exception clusters grouped by check id\par
\par
Grouping logic:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab group by `exception.checkId`\par
\tab\bullet\tab count occurrences\par
\tab\bullet\tab keep highest observed severity for the cluster\par
\tab\bullet\tab sort by count descending\par
\tab\bullet\tab show top 5 on dashboard\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 Recommended next action panel\b0\fs22\par
\par
Current logic:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab derive top 3 blocking checks from `snapshot.blockingIssues`\par
\tab\bullet\tab pass them into `TopBlockerActionList`\par
\tab\bullet\tab use `criticalBlockerOutcomes` as total critical denominator\par
\par
Navigation:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab clicking a blocker navigates to:\par
  - `/exceptions?dataset=<scope>&ruleId=<checkId>&sort=count_desc`\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 Severity context note\b0\fs22\par
\par
Purpose:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab explain why critical/high issues can dominate the portfolio\par
\par
Implementation:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab collapsed note using the existing `Collapsible` primitive\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs30 Fallback and Preview Behaviour\b0\fs22\par
\par
When no live signals exist:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab the dashboard renders empty states instead of misleading zeroes\par
\par
When preview snapshots are used:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `buildFallbackSnapshot()` injects non-live representative values\par
\par
Developers must ensure:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab live-truthful states do not silently fall back to preview values\par
\tab\bullet\tab scope absence uses neutral presentation\par
\tab\bullet\tab no KPI should show a failure state purely because a scenario is absent\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs30 Important Distinctions Developers Must Preserve\b0\fs22\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 Document count vs rule-outcome count\b0\fs22\par
\par
Never collapse these:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab invoices in scope\par
\tab\bullet\tab submission-ready invoices\par
\tab\bullet\tab critical blocker document count\par
\tab\bullet\tab total rule outcomes\par
\tab\bullet\tab critical blocker outcomes\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 Rule pass rate vs submission-ready rate\b0\fs22\par
\par
These must remain distinct:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab rule pass rate can be high even when many documents are not submission-ready\par
\tab\bullet\tab submission-ready rate is stricter because every executed rule must pass on a document\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 Scope absence vs poor performance\b0\fs22\par
\par
Examples:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab no credit notes in scope\par
\tab\bullet\tab no FX invoices in scope\par
\tab\bullet\tab no conditional-field-triggering documents in scope\par
\par
These should not render as red failure states.\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs30 Implementation Guidance\b0\fs22\par
\par
When adding a new dashboard metric:\par
\par
1. add or extend logic in `buildDashboardSnapshot()` or `computeDashboardMetrics()`\par
2. document:\par
   - meaning\par
   - exact formula\par
   - numerator\par
   - denominator\par
   - source fields\par
   - fallback logic\par
   - interpretation caveat\par
3. decide whether it is:\par
   - live only\par
   - preview-safe\par
   - scope-sensitive\par
4. add unit tests for:\par
   - normal case\par
   - empty case\par
   - divergence case if relevant\par
   - scope-absent case if relevant\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs30 Testing Guidance\b0\fs22\par
\par
Minimum test coverage expectations for dashboard metrics:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab document-vs-rule divergence\par
\tab\bullet\tab critical outcome vs critical document count\par
\tab\bullet\tab conditional completeness scope absence\par
\tab\bullet\tab URL deep-link filtering from blocker actions\par
\tab\bullet\tab no-preview fallback contamination when live signals exist\par
\par
Recommended future tests:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab explicit credit-note coverage permutations\par
\tab\bullet\tab AED vs foreign-currency mismatch scenarios\par
\tab\bullet\tab duplicate ratio edge cases\par
\tab\bullet\tab no invoice-linked exception fallback behavior\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs30 Known Gaps and Risks\b0\fs22\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 1. `ComplianceContext.getDashboardStats().passRate` is legacy-style\b0\fs22\par
\par
Current logic:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `(totalInvoices - invoicesWithExceptions) / totalInvoices`\par
\par
This is not the same thing as rule pass rate.\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 2. `Invalid Codelist` is heuristic\b0\fs22\par
\par
Current logic is text-based, not registry-backed.\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 3. `Critical Blocking Issues` label may still be interpreted as documents\b0\fs22\par
\par
The codebase now computes:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `criticalBlockerOutcomes`\par
\tab\bullet\tab `criticalBlockerDocumentCount`\par
\tab\bullet\tab `avgCriticalBlockersPerDocument`\par
\par
But the executive card itself still surfaces a critical issue count without fully disambiguating the semantic type.\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs24 4. Some readiness scores are product-level composites\b0\fs22\par
\par
They are useful decision-support metrics, but they are not legal formulas defined by PINT-AE or the FTA.\par
\par
\par\b\f1\fs30 Suggested Future Refactor\b0\fs22\par
\par
To make the dashboard easier to maintain, consider extracting:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab `src/components/dashboard/ExecutiveKPIs.tsx`\par
\tab\bullet\tab `src/components/dashboard/DataQualityKPIs.tsx`\par
\tab\bullet\tab `src/components/dashboard/UAECoverageKPIs.tsx`\par
\tab\bullet\tab `src/components/dashboard/ExceptionsPanel.tsx`\par
\tab\bullet\tab `src/lib/dashboard/buildDashboardSnapshot.ts`\par
\tab\bullet\tab `src/lib/dashboard/dashboardMetricDefinitions.ts`\par
\par
This would separate:\par
